{"id":"20260825T231835.973315998Z-48ad643c","time":"2026-08-25T23:18:35.973315998Z","session_id":"session-20260825T231615.541058032Z","task_id":"task-1787699775541276681","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  The transcript in internal/tui cannot be scrolled: once the conversation is longer than the window, earlier lines run off the top and there is no way to reach them.\n\nMake the transcript scrollable through the ordinary bubbletea surface. A transcript longer than the window must show its most recent lines and tell the reader that earlier ones exist; PgUp must reveal previously hidden lines; PgDn must return towards the newest; scrolling past the start must rest at the first line rather than running off it or emptying the screen; and a transcript that fits must claim nothing is hidden. How the window is tracked is yours to decide.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] Model.View currently wraps all transcript lines and permanently slices them to the newest rows that fit, leaving no retained viewport position. (internal/tui/model.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The ordinary key handling currently has no PgUp or PgDn transcript-navigation cases. (internal/tui/model.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] wrapRows already converts logical transcript entries into padded terminal rows, providing the row-level representation needed for viewport bounds. (internal/tui/model.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] internal/tui/scroll_test.go is absent from the current checkout and will be a new focused test file. (internal/tui/scroll_test.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei directly anchors the critical provider credential-ownership invariant to internal/tui/model.go and requires that it remain true. (internal/tui/model.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei reports no direct required tests or forbidden fixes for the two planned files. (internal/tui/model.go and internal/tui/scroll_test.go) — source: graph\n  [NEEDS EVIDENCE] A clamped offset over wrapped rows can satisfy scrolling and resizing without changing the transcript event model. (transcript viewport design) — source: inference\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: human-authority-required\n"}
